WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
A batch contains three images and their three associated captions.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Each image is compared with every text: matched pairs lie on the diagonal.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:22.617
The contrastive objective distinguishes those batch correspondences without guaranteeing every pair is correctly labelled.

4
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:29.967
We normalize two vectors and compare their angle using cosine similarity.

5
00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:36.817
Bringing their directions closer increases positive-pair similarity.

6
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:44.167
Training also contrasts other candidates; high cosine similarity is not a probability of truth.

7
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:51.517
Both captions name a circle and a square.

8
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:58.367
One places the circle on the left; the other places it on the right.

9
00:00:58.367 --> 00:01:05.717
Distinguishing them requires the relation, not just recognition of the object list.

10
00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:13.067
An image of three dots arrives paired with the caption “two dots”.

11
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:19.917
Treating that pair as positive favors a wrong correspondence.

12
00:01:19.917 --> 00:01:28.333
Review corrects or excludes the item; a larger batch alone does not eliminate this noise.

13
00:01:28.833 --> 00:01:35.683
A recording contains silence, a knock and another pause.

14
00:01:35.683 --> 00:01:42.850
A clip label says a knock is present but not when it starts or ends.

15
00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:50.200
A temporal annotation binds the event to the relevant interval with explicit boundaries.

16
00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:57.550
Image–text and image–audio pairs are trained around a shared concept.

17
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:04.400
The image can connect representations that were not directly paired.

18
00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:11.750
Test text–audio retrieval: a shared anchor does not guarantee equal quality for every relation.

